menu.GCS_Help_CHAR:
The Galaxy Challenge Season is a series of event quests held by the Galaxy Empire. When you complete these quests, you can get Tier Points to increase your Tier in the Season. Corresponding rewards can be claimed based on what Tier you reached this Season!

1. Tier Points: Can be obtained from completing daily quests, weekly quests, and seasonal quests;
2. Challenge Coins: Complete Challenge Season quests to earn valuable Challenge Coins. Challenge Coins can be used to get great rewards in the Challenge Trade Station;
3. Gift Swap: Complete Challenge Season quests to obtain the corresponding seasonal gift item. Send these gift items to other players get valuable rewards;
4. Challenge Trade Station: Limited-time exchange shop open only during Galaxy Challenge Season. Commanders can use Challenge Coins here to get premium items and limited-edition heroes;
5. Increase Season Tier: Every 10 Tier Points can be used to increase your Season Tier by 1;
6. Daily Quests: Up to 3 quests can be completed daily, and new quests will be available at 0:00 UTC daily until there are 3 quests. The quest won't reset if it hasn't been completed, or the rewards haven't been claimed. You can refresh one quest that you haven't completed for free every day;
7. Weekly Quest: When a Season starts, Weekly Quests will be available as the Season continues. Additional rewards can be obtained after completing the required amount of Weekly Quests that week;
8. Seasonal Quests: Available during the current Galaxy Challenge Season. Purchase the Season Pass to unlock these quests.
9. Purchase the Season Pass to enjoy the following bonuses:
a. Available Season Pass Quests: More quests will offer you more challenges along with more Tier Points! You can increase your Season Tier faster!
b. Available Season Pass Rewards: You can get all Pass Rewards that you have reached in the required Tiers! Also you can continue to increase your Season Tier to get more Pass Rewards!
c. Directly purchase Season Tiers: You can directly purchase Season Tiers so you can get all the rewards for this Season right now if you like!
10. The progression of the Purchase Credits Task is determined by the price of the pack and is not determined by the total credits get from the pack. For each price range corresponding credits, please refer to Empire Bank - Credits page.

help.CONTENT_1:
Cubit: The basic currency of Galaxy Empire. It’s a necessary resource for players to: upgrade buildings, enhance and upgrade equipment, compose Galactonite, repair ships, and reshape armor.

The main sources of Cubits:
1. Players can complete main tasks, daily tasks, collect from Citadel, send out diplomat Greenspan, complete primary battles and elite battles, participate in Arena, Infinite Cosmos, purchase daily packs, and use the Galaxy Slot to get Cubits;
2. Players can also participate in the daily PRIMUS event (event starts at 15:00 UTC) to get large amounts of Cubits. And there are also extra rewards of Cubits for 75% HP, 50% HP, 25%HP and for dealing the last blow. Event entrance is located in Dexter's Lab;
3. Players can also participate in the Primus Invasion event every Friday (event starts at 1:00 and 13:00 UTC) to get large amounts of Cubits. The event entrance is located in Dexter's Lab;
4. Mining is also a major source of Cubits. The Mine entrance is located in Dexter's Lab.

help.CONTENT_2:
Tech Points: The important energy used to upgrade technologies and increase Force. It can be used: At the Research Center to upgrade fleet technologies, In the Battle Training, located in Dexter's Lab, to enhance your Hull, or it can also be used to increase Force temporarily during the PRIMUS event. 

The main sources of Tech Points:
1. Players can send out diplomat Sonia, complete daily tasks, participate in Chaos Quasar, purchase daily packs, and use the Galaxy Slot to get Tech Points;
2. Players can participate in Arena to get a large amount of Tech Points;
3. Players can participate in weekly Pandora Cluster events to get a huge amount of Tech Points.  Event time: Saturday 2:00 am UTC - Tuesday 2:00 am UTC.

help.CONTENT_3:
Galactonite Energy: This precious energy can be used to upgrade Galactonite levels.

The main sources of Galactonite Energy:
1. Send out diplomat Sokolov;
2. Decompose your abandoned Galactonite;
3. Decompose Charged Galactonite, a new type of Galactonite which is available only during certain events or use the Galactonite Energy Black Market Pack.
4. Keep an eye on the Shop and Event Center as there is always a chance to purchase Galactonite Energy;
5. Mining is also a major source of Galactonite Energy. The Mine entrance is located in Dexter's Lab.

help.CONTENT_4:
Credit: Advanced currency of Galaxy Empire.

The main sources of Credits:
1. Login rewards and Month Cards;
2. Arena ranking rewards and rewards from certain battles;
3. Completing tasks and achievements;
4. Passing all battles of a constellation with a 3-Star rating;
5. Rush battles;
6. Purchasing Credits directly;
7. Closely following our facebook page to participate in forum events and get Credits;
8. Participating in Galaxy League;
9. Completing daily tasks and getting Credits from the progress bar rewards. （Galaxy servers）
10. Pandora Cluster Executive reward;. 
11. Ranking reward for Top 32 in Cross-Cosmos Competition.

help.CONTENT_5:
Dark Aerosiderite: It's a type of meteorolite rich in iron. It can be used to upgrade Components in Manoinver's Cabin.

The main sources of Dark Aerosiderites:
1. Participating in Forest of Stellar Territory to get a lot of Dark Aerosiderites;
2. Selling abandoned Legendary Equipment to get a certain amount of Dark Aerosiderite;
3. Keeping an eye on the Shop and Event Center for deals and then purchasing large amounts of Dark Aerosiderite.

help.CONTENT_7:
Class Chips: Contains Flagship Chips, Destroyer Chips, Rover Chips, Ranger Chips, Protector Chips, and Striker Chips. It's a precious item for Ship Augmentation.

The main sources of Class Chips:
1. Completing 10 Arena Battles daily to get a Class Chip Pack;
2. Players can get corresponding Class Chip Fragments from the weekly wormhole event (Monday to Saturday);
3. Each Ruling Star Reward in the Pandora Cluster will produce Class Chips of one type (Rover Chip, Ranger Chip, Protector Chip, Striker Chip);
4. Players can participate in Galaxy League to exchange all types of Class Chips;
5. Galaxy Slot will produce a small amount of Class Chip Fragments;
6. Keep an eye on the Shop and Event Center for purchasing Class Chips.

help.CONTENT_8:
Pandora Power Cores: Are a precious item used for ships' higher Augmentation levels.

The main sources of Pandora Power Cores:
1. Participating in Galaxy League and exchanging Pandora Power Cores;
2. Keeping an eye on the Shop, Black Market and Event Center to purchase Pandora Power Cores;
3. Participate in Primus Invasion and Conquer the Cosmos and get the top ranking;
4. Get Core Fragments from the first pass reward of Corridor of Time and Space;
5. Open Advanced Augmentation Packs and Pandora Packs.

help.CONTENT_9:
Pandora Power Crystals: Are precious items for ships' higher Augmentation levels.

The main sources of Pandora Power Crystals:
1. Participating in Galaxy League and exchanging Pandora Power Crystals;
2. Keeping an eye on the Shop, Black Market and Event Center to purchase Pandora Power Crystals;
3. Participate in Conquer the Cosmos and get the top ranking;
4. Get Crystal Fragments from the first pass reward of Corridor of Time and Space;
5. Open Advanced Augmentation Packs and Pandora Packs.

help.CONTENT_10:
Dexter Coins: Special coins that can be used in the Galaxy Slot to get abundant resources and items for free!

Main sources of Dexter Coins:
1. Daily login gifts containing 5 Dexter Coins. Don't forget to log into the game every day;
2. Level Up Gifts;
3. Main Task Completion Rewards.

help.CONTENT_12:
The ways to increase Force permanently:
1. Increase Fleet level;
2. Get new Ships from the Celestial Portal or events;
3. Enhance and upgrade Ship equipment in the Engineering Hub;
4. Upgrade Technology in the Research Center;
5. Equip high-rank Galactonite, and upgrade Galactonite level;
6. Reshape Armor in the Construction Yard;
7. Use Class Chips, Pandora Power Cores and Crystals to augment ships;
8. Adjust Ship Modules and save a better attribute bonus;
9. Use Z-Bosons to interfere with equipment;
10. Use Legendary Equipment in Manoinver's Cabin and upgrade Components with Dark Aerosiderites.

The ways to increase Force shortly and apply to systems:
1. Players can use Paintcoat to increase corresponding attributes for 24 hours; the bonus takes effect in story battles, elite battles, Arena, Pandora Cluster, Conquer the Cosmos and so on;
2. Players can participate in Galaxy League and get a bonus after each season (from 0:00 UTC 12th of each month to 23:59 UTC 11th of the next month); the bonus takes effect in story battles, elite battles, Arena, Pandora Cluster, Conquer the Cosmos and so on;
3. Daily Primus bonus starts at 14:58 UTC. The bonus only takes effect in Primus;
4. A Temporary bonus will start for Primus Invasion every Friday. The bonus only takes effect in Primus Invasion.

help.CONTENT_13:
Attack Order: Ships in the front row attack first. Ships in the same row attack from left to right;
Target Order: Attack the ship of the same line in the front first. If there are no ships in the same line, then attack ships of the adjoining line;

Player attack order depends on players' total speed. If both sides have the same speed, then the attacker will attack first.

How to increase Speed:
1. Level up ships;
2. Upgrade Basic Engine, Enhanced Engine, Advanced Engine and Extra Dimensional Engine in the Research Center;
3. Put ships with better speed attributes in Form
4. Equip Speed Galactonite
5. Complete collections in League of Heroes;
6. When Violette[+4] is in Form as a Lieutenant, the total speed will increase by 100* [The number of Rovers in Form].
7. When John is in Form as a Lieutenant, each ship's speed will increase by 10 in battle.

help.CONTENT_17:
1. Every 30 minutes the supply will automatically recover by 1 point if the total supply is under 20 points; 
2. Daily Login Packs will provide 5 supply points. So don't forget to log into the game every day;
3. Some Active Pack rewards contain supplies;
4. There's a chance to get supply items from the Galaxy Slot;
5. Players can purchase supply before taking part in a battle;
6. Each time a player levels up, the supply will be restored to 20 points if the player has less than 20 points of Supply. 
7. Participate in Primus Invasion and get the top ranking.

help.CONTENT_18:
Players can use Plans to upgrade corresponding equipment in the Engineering Hub. Each upgrade will reduce 5 enhancement levels.

The main sources of Plans:
1. Challenging elite opponents in the Conservatory;
2. Purchase Plan Packs of different levels from the Shop with Credits;
3. There is a chance to get Plans from the Galaxy Slot.

help.MEDAL_GLORY_1:
1. There are some Honor Combinations in each Medal Archive. After Honor Combination activation and star up, you can enjoy great stats bonus. The stats bonus will take effect for all ships;
2. Each Honor Combination activation and star up will consume corresponding medals, at the same time you can get a certain amount of Honor Points. The detailed rules are as the following: For each blue medal consumed, you can get 1 Honor Point; For each purple medal consumed, you can get 8 Honor Points; For each golden medal consumed, you can get 50 Honor Points; For each red medal consumed, you can get 90 Honor Points;
3. When the Honor Points have reached the requirements, you can get stats bonus reward from [Achievements]. And you will have to tap [Activate] button manually to make it take effect. The obtained stats bonus can also take effect on all ships;
4. You can also get back the consumed medals in Honor Combination activation and star up from the reset function in Medal Archives.
5. In Medal Archives, only unequipped medals of rank 4 or below rank 4 can be used in activation and star up.

help.MEDAL_GLORY_2:
1. Honor Combination activation and star up will provide you with a lot of stats bonus which will take effect on all ships. Please note that only unequipped medals of rank 4 or below rank 4 can be used in Honor Combination activation and star up.
2. Each Honor Combination activation and star up will consume corresponding medals, at the same time you can get a certain amount of Honor Points. The detailed rules are as the following: For each blue medal consumed, you can get 1 Honor Point; For each purple medal consumed, you can get 8 Honor Points; For each golden medal consumed, you can get 50 Honor Points; For each red medal consumed, you can get 90 Honor Points;
3. You can use [Reset] function to make Honor Combinations become inactivated. At the same time, you shall get all the consumed medals in Honor Combinations back;
4. You can use [Preview] function to check the obtained stats bonus from Honor Combination activation and star up.
